---
description: UI component and styling conventions
globs: "**/*.{ts,tsx,css,module.css}"
alwaysApply: true
---

UI components should be semantic, accessible, and minimal.

Reusable UI components must not contain business logic.

Theme variables live in `@ui/common/src/theme/specifications.ts`.

### Web
- Use CSS modules.
- Class names use kebab-case.
- Prefer `className` over inline `style`.
- Use inline `style` only for runtime-computed values that cannot be expressed with CSS classes or CSS variables.
- Use CSS variables for theming.
- Never use `!important`.

### Mobile
- Use `StyleSheet.create` for styles.
- Do not use CSS modules or CSS custom properties.